{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not","id":774231,"title":"Heroes don't have a Supernatural Resistance Trait, right? So, why not?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-25T13:25:16-08:00","id":774231,"title":"Heroes don't have a Supernatural Resistance Trait, right? So, why not?","content":"Similar to the &quot;hunters are too weak&quot; thread that's going around: Are hunters supposed to have a supernatural resistance trait that we're just missing? Currently it seems that a Beast with high Satiety could just nightmare the EFF out of any Hunter and end the fight almost instantly. Are we missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9850-bestopheles-gmail-com","name":"[email\u00a0protected]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T13:28:09-08:00","id":774237,"title":"","content":"A lil more data: We're playing in a werewolf crossover game. Two beasts and one wolf. The Beasts were attacked by a mob with a hunter. The wolf shifted, mob went into lunacy (most of whom ran away), and the Hunter barely kept his stuff together due to high integrity. Then Hunter got hit with a nightmare and got creamed. All of us were a bit shocked by the quick resolution, and wondering if we'd misplayed the rules a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9850-bestopheles-gmail-com","name":"[email\u00a0protected]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T13:54:37-08:00","id":774256,"title":"","content":"I use Conviction from Mirrors as a power stat for Hunter, as it plays in really well with the stuff they can do with Willpower. It also provides supernatural tolerance, but not on a 1:1 basis.<br /> <br /> That said, Heroes aren't Hunters. If they don't have a supernatural tolerance stat, I wouldn't give them one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T20:35:40-08:00","id":774509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=774256#post774256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use Conviction from Mirrors as a power stat for Hunter, as it plays in really well with the stuff they can do with Willpower. It also provides supernatural tolerance, but not on a 1:1 basis.<br /> <br /> That said, Heroes aren't Hunters. If they don't have a supernatural tolerance stat, I wouldn't give them one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seen that on my copy of Mirrors. I've been thinking of doing a mechanics hack on it, which I'll probably get to when I have time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T20:53:48-08:00","id":774517,"title":"","content":"I think that's kind of the point. A Hero is a cocky, vainglorious sonuvabitch (for the most part), but all they really have are their Anathema. They &quot;cheat&quot; to gain the upper hand against Beasts, and they'll go down against any other threat immediately.<br /> <br /> As for Hunters, I'd say that Tier-1 Hunters should be considered normal humans, but Conspiracy or Compact Status should offer a Supernatural Tolerance (Especially supernatural compacts/conspiracies, like the Lucifuge).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:41:35-08:00","id":774539,"title":"","content":"In addition to using Conviction as a power stat for Hunters, it was also opt-in in my games. Any Hunter could choose to take on The Vigil and gain Conviction. Plus side is having a power stat. Downside is that now, you will be on The Vigil forever. Aside from the narrative consequences of never being able to 'retire', you also can't be turned into a vampire to save your life when you're bleeding out, or awaken as a mage, or be brought back by a Geist.<br /> <br /> In most games that wouldn't be much of a consequence (although the narrative consequence is pretty heavy), but everything I run is very crossover heavy.<br /> <br /> I allowed any hunter to make that decision, or not make it, Tier isn't the best kind of judge for that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:50:33-08:00","id":776220,"title":"","content":"Two options spring to mind.<br /> <br /> Create a defensive gift to give some protection from nightmares.<br /> <br /> Rule that indomitable adds its bonus against nightmares, and have more dangerous heroes buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:52:21-08:00","id":776360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong><a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection\" class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"60020513140f1008050c051320070d01090c4e030f0d\">[email&#160;protected]</a></strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=774237#post774237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lil more data: We're playing in a werewolf crossover game. Two beasts and one wolf. The Beasts were attacked by a mob with a hunter. The wolf shifted, mob went into lunacy (most of whom ran away), and the Hunter barely kept his stuff together due to high integrity. Then Hunter got hit with a nightmare and got creamed. All of us were a bit shocked by the quick resolution, and wondering if we'd misplayed the rules a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mob would have gotten extreme bonuses to said lunacy roll. There's a reason that Iron Masters are the quintessential wolves in sheep's clothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:55:19-08:00","id":776362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=776220#post776220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Rule that indomitable adds its bonus against nightmares, and have more dangerous heroes buy it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that as if it didn't already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T07:52:49-08:00","id":776581,"title":"","content":"I don't think that heroes are meant to be equal challenges to a beast. In many ways, Beast is the opposite of Hunter as a game. In HtV, you're playing the ones standing up for humanity against the darkness. You track down monsters, slay them, question if certain monsters deserve to be put down for monsters (VanHellsing crimes), question if you've become the monsters you've fought against. You leverage numbers, tactics, banes, and whatever minor magics you can learn against the monsters. In BtP, you play the monster that's being hunted, attacked, questioned, and see the hunters as the monster they claim the Begotten is. The same tactics are used for both hunters and heroes (I'm going to actually argue that being a hero is equivalent to being in a Conspiracy similar to the Lucifuge). <br /> <br /> If you make heroes into equal challenges to the monsters, you undercut a lot of the themes of the game. The heroes aren't meant to be equals to the monsters. They're the underdogs suffering from misunderstanding, ignorance, and compulsions. Do you just kill them and feed your Hunger? Teach them Lessons and have them grow up? Decide that the heroes have become the equivalent of Slashers and put them down? You have the power here. You are supposed to look down at the heroes as mere mortals that you can take down with a simple Nightmare or Atavism. You're supposed to feel you have all the time in the world, because what can they really do to you? Monsters in stories look down on the plucky underdog heroes for a reason - they're the underdogs. They underestimate them. Then, out comes the banes and the magic and the followers, and you fight. You likely even win, but you are forced to use power to do so. Suddenly, you're Starving. Dying of hunger, lashing out.<br /> <br /> The heroes aren't the equal-and-opposite opponents. They're not the enemies you go fist-to-fist with. That would be your fellow Children and other supernaturals. The vampire priest, the werewolf cop, the mage engineer, the fae broker that oppose your feedings, or try to subvert you to their own causes. They're the sirens and gorgons and dragons that come after your collection or your prey, that undermine your Hunger and steal your Lair. <br /> <br /> <br /> Heroes fill a necessary niche in Beast. They make you question if you really are the monster they accuse you of being. They do not provide a white room fighting matchup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T08:29:49-08:00","id":777160,"title":"","content":"MCN, I think you've pretty well summed up my thoughts on Heroes. Though it's worth noting that old, successful Heroes can be pretty scary combatants.<br /> <br /> I had an idea about a Highlander-esque group of Heroes who have lived for centuries through killing lots of Beasts. They meet up and share their war stories and trophies and occasionally group up to take out broods or powerful Begotten. They've got cults and organizations of hunters that have sprung up around them. They're the 1% of Heroes who take the fight to beasts but don't fall victim to their own hubris.<br /> <br /> 9 times out of 10 Heroes will be puny mortals who couldn't hope to stand against a beast in a fair fight. That 10th Hero makes the beast sweat a bit and say, &quot;H-how!? This is impossible!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T19:02:55-08:00","id":777490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=776362#post776362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You say that as if it didn't already.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I typed it like it doesn't say one way or another, so it's the ST's call, because the book doesn't say so one way or another. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T21:08:35-08:00","id":777529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=777490#post777490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I typed it like it doesn't say one way or another, so it's the ST's call, because the book doesn't say so one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sword, Indomitable's mechanical effect is literally &quot;apply a bonus to your innate means of resisting supernatural mental influence&quot; and Nightmares are literally the supernatural mental influence powers of the Begotten. This is the opposite of ambiguous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T06:59:00-08:00","id":777728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong><a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection\" class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"ff9d9a8c8b908f979a939a8cbf98929e9693d19c9092\">[email&#160;protected]</a></strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not#post774231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar to the &amp;quot;hunters are too weak&amp;quot; thread that's going around: Are hunters supposed to have a supernatural resistance trait that we're just missing? Currently it seems that a Beast with high Satiety could just nightmare the EFF out of any Hunter and end the fight almost instantly. Are we missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me start by saying how awesome I think Hunter is. I don't think you're missing anything. However, I do think you're onto something. My solution is a hack into that adds a supernatural advantage trait to Hunter. I call it Initiation. It also adds dice to your combat pools when used against a particular kind of supernatural (all Hunters are specialists). Unfortunately, every dot after the first one reduces your maximum Integrity by 1. If you hit 0 Integrity for some reason, you become a Slasher. <br /> <br /> Basically I wanted to add some level of moral dilemma to the game. This is realized by Hunters becoming more callous as they become more initiated in their calling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:53:48-08:00","id":777952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=777529#post777529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sword, Indomitable's mechanical effect is literally &quot;apply a bonus to your innate means of resisting supernatural mental influence&quot; and Nightmares are literally the supernatural mental influence powers of the Begotten. This is the opposite of ambiguous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem. Page 133-<br /> <br /> &quot;While Nightmares are \u201call in your head\u201d in the sense that only the victim experiences the effects and sees the<br /> hallucinations, that\u2019s not the same thing as Nightmares being \u201cillusionary\u201d or somehow \u201cnot real.\u201d The effects of Nightmares<br /> are very real and are quite capable of inflicting somatic injury or even death. Just because no one else can see the bugs crawling<br /> all over you doesn\u2019t mean they aren\u2019t there.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> So nightmares are both hallucinatory and real, would you like to rethink your comment about it not being ambiguous? <br /> <br /> And if nightmares are mental influences, then just how can behold my true form turn someone into a statue of stone or salt? You cannot kill it turns the damage from a flamethrower or a machinegun into bashing damage, how is that a mental influence? <br /> <br /> If they're hallucinatory, then yes indomitable would help against them. If they're real, then where does it say that indomitable makes it harder for bugs to bite you or adds dice to resist petrification? <br /> <br /> The book says they're both, so I stand by my statement that it's up to the ST as to whether it helps or not. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T16:08:08-08:00","id":777959,"title":"","content":"Sword, you are equating &quot;mental attack&quot; to mean &quot;not real.&quot; No one is saying that. The bugs in question are Astral bugs attacking. Goetic beings are real, but they are also 100% mental attacks. They can be both.<br /> <br /> Its the type of thing in stories, where a psychic makes you hallucinate that you're on fire, so that you actually manifest the signs of burns from such a powerful hallucination. That's how Nightmares operate. Its real to the person being attacked, but it still entirely in the head. It says it right in the section you quoted. Nightmares are all in your head, but that doesn't mean its not real. Ergo, its both in your head and real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T17:58:38-08:00","id":778007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=777952#post777952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahem. Page 133-<br /> <br /> &quot;While Nightmares are \u201call in your head\u201d in the sense that only the victim experiences the effects and sees the<br /> hallucinations, that\u2019s not the same thing as Nightmares being \u201cillusionary\u201d or somehow \u201cnot real.\u201d The effects of Nightmares<br /> are very real and are quite capable of inflicting somatic injury or even death. Just because no one else can see the bugs crawling<br /> all over you doesn\u2019t mean they aren\u2019t there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd been given to understand that Nightmares were not so much induced hallucinations as they were conducting power from the Primordial Dream to manifest horrible, horrible things that only the victim can actually see or feel. I figured it's a bit like Freddy Krueger and how he kills people in their dreams -- it's an attack that happens in their minds, but because of weird Dream Magic, the damage he inflicts to them is real damage that actually does manifest on their bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T18:19:06-08:00","id":778010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=777952#post777952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So nightmares are both hallucinatory and real, would you like to rethink your comment about it not being ambiguous?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p122</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Direct emotional and mental influence is the realm of Nightmares</b>, not Atavisms.</div> </div> </div> </div>to say<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p144</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although <b>Nightmares are constructs of mind and soul</b>, those that target fears of the body, like health, attractiveness, or injury, are contested with Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div>no.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p143</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather, by establishing Family Ties with another monster, the Beast may reach deep into the Primordial Dream to draw forth a nugget of the fear that monster represents <b>and make it manifest in the mind of her victim.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If your argument was founded on Behold, My True Form!, then you have expressed yourself very poorly by generalizing that statement as &quot;[Indomitable might not apply against] all Nightmares.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p116</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character possesses an iron will. <b>The powers of the supernatural have little bearing on her behavior.</b> She can stand up to a vampire\u2019s mind control, a witch\u2019s charms, or a ghost\u2019s gifts of fright. <b>Any time a supernatural creature uses a power to influence your character\u2019s thoughts or emotions</b>, add two dice to the dice pool to contest it.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T18:28:28-08:00","id":778732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774231-heroes-don-t-have-a-supernatural-resistance-trait-right-so-why-not?p=777728#post777728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me start by saying how awesome I think Hunter is. I don't think you're missing anything. However, I do think you're onto something. My solution is a hack into that adds a supernatural advantage trait to Hunter. I call it Initiation. It also adds dice to your combat pools when used against a particular kind of supernatural (all Hunters are specialists). Unfortunately, every dot after the first one reduces your maximum Integrity by 1. If you hit 0 Integrity for some reason, you become a Slasher.<br /> <br /> Basically I wanted to add some level of moral dilemma to the game. This is realized by Hunters becoming more callous as they become more initiated in their calling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrity is not Morality. The Moral-Relativism in Vigil was handled by the mechanics for changing your Threshold Sins back in first edition, which later got ported into Danse Macabre for Requiem 1.0. In Second, mundane humans get to write their Morals and Ethics from scratch, with a few provisos (no killing being a big one), so building a monster-hunter is largely a question of experience (i.e.: Conspiracy and Compact-Level Hunters should have earned commensurately more permissive Breaking Points than those of a green, Street-level Hunter).<br /> <br /> I think that what are more-or-less mundane people getting Power Stats from day one isn't exactly appropriate, but if I didn't, I'd lean more toward forcing Breaking Points around SRT 2, with growing penalties once your players start hitting 5 and up, rather than an Integrity Cap. This way, you have room to crawl back from the edge without railroading people to Slasher territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T19:50:34-08:00","id":778773,"title":"","content":"I can see why you'd do that. I'll admit that it's probably more playable than what I'm doing but, I was aiming for dynamic closer to Vampire's Blood Potency. In my Hunter chronicles, there is a simple truth that everyone at higher levels of Initiation realize. Monsters are made by people, when there are no people then there will be no monsters. The fight against the supernatural ends up being a fight against humanity. <br /> <br /> Regarding morals and Integrity, please see a theory that most contemporary philosophers hate, moral relativism. World of Darkness's Integrity boils down to moral relativism exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}